	<RecipeDef ParentName="Make_IcecreamBase" Class="UniversalFermenterSK.RecipeDef_UF">
		<defName>Make_IceCreamfruits</defName>
	    <label>Ice Cream(fruits) x2</label>
        <description>*"When Imperial nutritionists declared synthetic paste to be "a perfectly balanced food" for the 57th time, the colonists responded by choking on these multi-colored ice balls. Supposedly "natural" - although every child knows that real fruit died out before the Fall Wars.The secret ingredient is nostalgia. And 12% genetically modified pseudo-strawberries grown in underground hydroponic jars (which are, of course, completely legal and definitely do not require monthly "donations" to the local branch of the Imperial Inspectorate)."*</description>
		<ingredients>
			<li>
				<filter>
					<thingDefs>
						<li>Milk</li>
					</thingDefs>
				</filter>
				<count>6</count>
			</li>
			<li>
				<filter>
					<thingDefs>
						<li>RawBerries</li>
					</thingDefs>
				</filter>
				<count>1</count>
			</li>
		</ingredients>
		<fixedIngredientFilter>
			<thingDefs>
			<li>Milk</li>
			<li>RawBerries</li>
			</thingDefs>
		</fixedIngredientFilter>
		<products>
			<IceCreamfruits>2</IceCreamfruits>
		</products>
	</RecipeDef>

	<RecipeDef ParentName="Make_IcecreamBase" Class="UniversalFermenterSK.RecipeDef_UF">
		<defName>Make_IceCreamchocolate</defName>
		<label>Ice Cream(chocolate) x2</label>
		<description>*"Officially approved by the Imperial Committee on People's Happiness (Protocol #451-bis) as a "morally necessary substance for the productivity of colonists". Each serving contains:*
*- 12% genetically modified cocoa from Outer Rim plantations (flamethrower-treated for sterility)*
*- 43% recycled milk concentrate (don't ask what it's made of)*
*- 22% crystals of happiness (chemical formula classified by order of the Architect)*
*- 23% government propaganda (in the form of crispy waffle patterns)*
Recent studies have shown that 97% of colonist subjects demonstrated temporary loyalty after consumption. The remaining 3% were... recycled into the next batch."</description>
		<ingredients>
			<li>
				<filter>
					<thingDefs>
						<li>Milk</li>
					</thingDefs>
				</filter>
				<count>6</count>
			</li>
			<li>
				<filter>
					<thingDefs>
						<li>Chocolate</li>
